{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "023A", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-equivalence}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:627458b47485a3c6af89a351c835467df42ba58db50c418c952a8890fa5fc299", "source_text": "Descent data for quasi-coherent sheaves", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c2b1a9547692811b282be2b63c86e4fdfa07589d999364ae142f035a4af589d6", "unit_id": "tag:023A:title"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "023A", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\text{pr}_i : X \\times \\ldots \\times X \\to X$", "MATH_0002": "$i = 0$", "MATH_0003": "$\\text{pr}_0, \\text{pr}_1 : X \\times X  \\to X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\text{pr}_0, \\text{pr}_1, \\text{pr}_2 : X \\times X \\times X  \\to X$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ca467d8344644bab94506c8a40198af69e59ea38299faade92bd3dd3fc6531f6", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:20108ed6345fe32d460a45996656c4c47903a58191f180ebe937f54d2624f1a8", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this chapter we will use the convention where\nthe projection maps <MATH_0001>\nare labeled starting with <MATH_0002>. Hence we have\n<MATH_0003>,\n<MATH_0004>,\netc.\n\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:11d025335a36c383b83cbd9dde89fd2354929bffb1d5a220b56e65c9b884228c", "unit_id": "tag:023A:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "023A", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\{f_i : S_i \\to S\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$(\\mathcal{F}_i, \\varphi_{ij})$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F}_i$", "MATH_0006": "$S_i$", "MATH_0007": "$i \\in I$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{O}_{S_i \\times_S S_j}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\varphi_{ij} : \\text{pr}_0^*\\mathcal{F}_i \\to \\text{pr}_1^*\\mathcal{F}_j$", "MATH_0010": "$(i, j) \\in I^2$", "MATH_0011": "$(i, j, k) \\in I^3$", "MATH_0012": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\text{pr}_0^*\\mathcal{F}_i \\ar[rd]_{\\text{pr}_{01}^*\\varphi_{ij}}\n\\ar[rr]_{\\text{pr}_{02}^*\\varphi_{ik}} & &\n\\text{pr}_2^*\\mathcal{F}_k \\\\\n& \\text{pr}_1^*\\mathcal{F}_j \\ar[ru]_{\\text{pr}_{12}^*\\varphi_{jk}} &\n}\n$$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{O}_{S_i \\times_S S_j \\times_S S_k}$", "MATH_0014": "$\\psi : (\\mathcal{F}_i, \\varphi_{ij}) \\to\n(\\mathcal{F}'_i, \\varphi'_{ij})$", "MATH_0015": "$\\psi = (\\psi_i)_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0016": "$\\mathcal{O}_{S_i}$", "MATH_0017": "$\\psi_i : \\mathcal{F}_i \\to \\mathcal{F}'_i$", "MATH_0018": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\text{pr}_0^*\\mathcal{F}_i \\ar[r]_{\\varphi_{ij}} \\ar[d]_{\\text{pr}_0^*\\psi_i}\n& \\text{pr}_1^*\\mathcal{F}_j \\ar[d]^{\\text{pr}_1^*\\psi_j} \\\\\n\\text{pr}_0^*\\mathcal{F}'_i \\ar[r]^{\\varphi'_{ij}} &\n\\text{pr}_1^*\\mathcal{F}'_j \\\\\n}\n$$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0003": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0003": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-descent-datum-quasi-coherent}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5596a0ba2ebcb87ce7cb8271036f15b209bdcdb39e0393e1a7af7409beda8170", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6fcd24a9286c429afd1cae6c39cd3d12d9bda2e631c62cdb074bbb76fcafde01", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a family\nof morphisms with target <MATH_0003>.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> A <TEXTITOPEN_0001>descent datum <MATH_0004>\nfor quasi-coherent sheaves<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> with respect to the given family\nis given by a quasi-coherent sheaf <MATH_0005> on <MATH_0006> for\neach <MATH_0007>, an isomorphism of quasi-coherent\n<MATH_0008>-modules\n<MATH_0009>\nfor each pair <MATH_0010>\nsuch that for every triple of indices <MATH_0011> the\ndiagram\n<MATH_0012>\nof <MATH_0013>-modules\ncommutes. This is called the <TEXTITOPEN_0002>cocycle condition<TEXTITCLOSE_0002>.\n<STRUCT_0003> A <TEXTITOPEN_0003>morphism <MATH_0014> of descent data<TEXTITCLOSE_0003> is given\nby a family <MATH_0015> of morphisms of\n<MATH_0016>-modules <MATH_0017>\nsuch that all the diagrams\n<MATH_0018>\ncommute.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:434acb0298234f389cd9b22a70fe05b10da476a20ac2ea64c3ea5ae8a906006b", "unit_id": "tag:023B:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "023A", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S = \\bigcup S_i$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$\\{S_i \\to S\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\{S \\to S\\}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\text{id}_S$", "MATH_0006": "$(\\mathcal{F}, \\text{id}_\\mathcal{F})$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sheaves-section-glueing-sheaves}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5ce743a52275d0e69546201d8bbe4a21623e9d7f3b936c7deb30e56b231edeeb", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1d1e6ea4cf3a1cb319965bc098c8e40aba9426dab5b8ba9fdabb398b1fa7b7fc", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nA good example to keep in mind is the following.\nSuppose that <MATH_0001> is an open covering.\nIn that case we have seen descent data for sheaves of sets in\nSheaves, Section <REF_0001>\nwhere we called them ``glueing data for sheaves of sets\nwith respect to the given covering''. Moreover, we proved\nthat the category of glueing data is equivalent to the category\nof sheaves on <MATH_0002>. We will show the analogue in the setting above when\n<MATH_0003> is an fpqc covering.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nIn the extreme case where the covering <MATH_0004>\nis given by <MATH_0005> a descent datum is necessarily\nof the form <MATH_0006>. The cocycle\ncondition guarantees that the identity on <MATH_0007> is the\nonly permitted map in this case. The following lemma shows\nin particular that to every quasi-coherent sheaf of\n<MATH_0008>-modules there is associated a unique\ndescent datum with respect to any given family.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:07da8635b87ef6c0e1d4a4da845be937bded8a6465c9d3002add9b615b51e423", "unit_id": "tag:023A:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "023A", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{U} = \\{U_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{V} = \\{V_j \\to V\\}_{j \\in J}$", "MATH_0003": "$(g, \\alpha : I \\to J, (g_i)) : \\mathcal{U} \\to \\mathcal{V}$", "MATH_0004": "$(\\mathcal{F}_j, \\varphi_{jj'})$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{V_j \\to V\\}_{j \\in J}$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\left(g_i^*\\mathcal{F}_{\\alpha(i)},\n(g_i \\times g_{i'})^*\\varphi_{\\alpha(i)\\alpha(i')}\\right)\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0008": "$(\\mathcal{F}_j, \\varphi_{jj'})$", "MATH_0009": "$(g', \\alpha' : I \\to J, (g'_i))$", "MATH_0010": "$g = g'$", "MATH_0011": "$$\n(g_i^*\\mathcal{F}_{\\alpha(i)},\n(g_i \\times g_{i'})^*\\varphi_{\\alpha(i)\\alpha(i')})\n\\cong\n((g'_i)^*\\mathcal{F}_{\\alpha'(i)},\n(g'_i \\times g'_{i'})^*\\varphi_{\\alpha'(i)\\alpha'(i')}).\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-definition-morphism-coverings}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-refine-descent-datum}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ae7d4815672e6cf7d65642914979e6d3a894b86500585e5c3e0bb13f3b10143d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2f62526602e1a387465dfc8f1124501170196cc0d9c1e0d08813a457d13ff55c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> and\n<MATH_0002>\nbe families of morphisms of schemes with fixed target.\nLet <MATH_0003>\nbe a morphism of families of maps with fixed target, see\nSites, Definition <REF_0001>.\nLet <MATH_0004> be a descent\ndatum for quasi-coherent sheaves with respect to the\nfamily <MATH_0005>. Then\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The system\n<MATH_0006>\nis a descent datum with respect to the family <MATH_0007>.\n<STRUCT_0003> This construction is functorial in the descent datum\n<MATH_0008>.\n<STRUCT_0004> Given a second morphism <MATH_0009>\nof families of maps with fixed target with <MATH_0010>\nthere exists a functorial isomorphism of descent data\n<MATH_0011>\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:db3a60ae86218d8dcd1fc04cedc7197beee5988a2ea76488255fe43edebcc05e", "unit_id": "tag:023C:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "023A", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$g_i^*\\mathcal{F}_{\\alpha(i)} \\to (g'_i)^*\\mathcal{F}_{\\alpha'(i)}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\varphi_{\\alpha(i)\\alpha'(i)}$", "MATH_0003": "$(g_i, g'_i) : U_i \\to V_{\\alpha(i)} \\times_V V_{\\alpha'(i)}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f6f6917f4b041b74fa069f99929f8395344798a6db0872610d6a3f0a3954a7bd", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5d6e44e0776e531e1e469911e9019c8f0399e9e750b56b51c8c7e0288e3f03b1", "source_text": "Omitted. Hint: The maps\n<MATH_0001>\nwhich give the isomorphism of descent data in part (3)\nare the pullbacks of the maps <MATH_0002> by the\nmorphisms <MATH_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:70aef1d081c266fc1ebead1f263dae25164cabf09bcc354b2b2463a4ea66d72e", "unit_id": "tag:023C:proof"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "023A", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{U} = \\{S_i \\to S\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\{S \\to S\\}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "MATH_0005": "$(\\mathcal{F}|_{S_i}, can)$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{U}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ebdbaa203ecf72b5f16e6337327e1815d21448a7a5e8a85afe8ac3ceb902ba0c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c251b03a01d3ddc570bf91bab93366b4c4bb61b984b3e2a6cba7a21370bc95b6", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nAny family <MATH_0001> is a refinement of\nthe trivial covering <MATH_0002> in a unique way. For\na quasi-coherent sheaf <MATH_0003> on <MATH_0004> we denote simply\n<MATH_0005> the descent datum with respect to\n<MATH_0006> obtained by the procedure above.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9fbe779fd0ffe599cd5dbe0294d018d22e6a86e7a0e4b36fab6584ad591b36ad", "unit_id": "tag:023A:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "023A", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\{S_i \\to S\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\{S \\to S\\}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\{S_i \\to S\\}$", "MATH_0009": "$(\\mathcal{F}|_{S_i}, can)$", "MATH_0010": "$(\\mathcal{F}_i, \\varphi_{ij})$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0012": "$S$", "MATH_0013": "$(\\mathcal{F}_i, \\varphi_{ij})$", "MATH_0014": "$(\\mathcal{F}|_{S_i}, can)$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0003": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0003": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-descent-datum-effective-quasi-coherent}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b5aea0114108dd131f12f0f663ac2f40c7a3b41c350f4f3b905d330d32600931", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:adae88fb03f22a18e9c544fdcf5ed6fce0de13de203b26ca49be95210ec14a0c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a family of morphisms\nwith target <MATH_0003>.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> Let <MATH_0004> be a quasi-coherent <MATH_0005>-module.\nWe call the unique descent on <MATH_0006> datum with respect to the covering\n<MATH_0007> the <TEXTITOPEN_0001>trivial descent datum<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>.\n<STRUCT_0003> The pullback of the trivial descent datum to\n<MATH_0008> is called the <TEXTITOPEN_0002>canonical descent datum<TEXTITCLOSE_0002>.\nNotation: <MATH_0009>.\n<STRUCT_0004> A descent datum <MATH_0010>\nfor quasi-coherent sheaves with respect to the given covering\nis said to be <TEXTITOPEN_0003>effective<TEXTITCLOSE_0003> if there exists a quasi-coherent\nsheaf <MATH_0011> on <MATH_0012> such that <MATH_0013>\nis isomorphic to <MATH_0014>.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d9c95ce9e14bb7b87965125cc53bdf60b1ed5061a4c2c42da00b56c300e8d55c", "unit_id": "tag:023D:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "023A", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$S = \\bigcup U_i$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{U} = \\{U_i \\to S\\}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{U}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-zariski-descent-effective}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8f298c043b4c6b685a757e1359dedcdff103a3e1bb8b2993f4950f25edd3ff2c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6703ca4892e79258705f90e6d6266edd6956276a336a03e5980cd0e7c9902149", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be an open covering.\nAny descent datum on quasi-coherent sheaves\nfor the family <MATH_0003> is\neffective. Moreover, the functor from the category of\nquasi-coherent <MATH_0004>-modules to the category\nof descent data with respect to <MATH_0005> is fully faithful.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:38a43dcd3658959d655074f2b41e02dfe772947914247a027fc67a4500130217", "unit_id": "tag:023E:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "023A", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{sheaves-section-glueing-sheaves}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{modules-definition-quasi-coherent}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5bc9012ef72d8a53cda95b3765658c16c028da207084057fe22e4ddb2813bf2c", "source_text": "This follows immediately from\nSheaves, Section <REF_0001>\nand the fact that being quasi-coherent is a local property, see\nModules, Definition <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b647279c21743f95c694ad5d21f66d048d1b0bb111b0e2624785f2fea4a09363", "unit_id": "tag:023E:proof"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "023A", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3573691b2509a0f8aa70ce98ec0c149710aa064347ad1e368b07c1faf12bc051", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nTo prove more we first need to study the case of modules over rings.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b521ee9f1725965260f54c82a3dc7e78a42e084e116e64e061095e73b836ac22", "unit_id": "tag:023A:prose-0004"}
